    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0529" n="1363" xml:id="pg1363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659a.119/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-23T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6673. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 124. Your 8540, February 6. Our 88, February 11,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d428-f1"/> notified you of our refusal license imports of wool.
                    Hereafter will hold all export and import licenses of Icelandic products pending
                    your negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
